---
title: Patty Melt
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, beef, cheese, bread
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Heat a #skillet{} over high heat to warm up, then reduce to medium heat. Add half of the @butter{2%tbsp} and toast @white bread{2%slices} on both sides until golden. Remove the bread and set aside.

Finely slice @brown onion{0.5}. Add @oil{1%tbsp}, the remaining @&butter, the sliced onion, and a pinch of @salt to the skillet. Cook over medium-high heat, stirring constantly, until caramelized. Transfer the onions directly onto one slice of toasted bread.

In a #small bowl{}, combine @mayonnaise{2%tbsp}, @chipotle in adobo{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{0.25%tsp}, @mustard powder{0.25%tsp}, @black pepper{0.25%tsp}, @white pepper{0.25%tsp}, @msg{1%pinch}, and @white distilled vinegar{1%tsp} to make the sauce.

Shape @beef mince{200%g} into two loose balls. Return the skillet to high heat and season the pan with a pinch of @salt. Place the beef balls in the pan, season the tops with more @&salt, and let sear for ~{30%seconds}. Press flat with a #burger smasher{}.

Cook the patties for ~{2%minutes}, flip them, and top each with a slice of @cheese{2%slices} to melt.

Spread the sauce over both slices of toasted bread. Place the patties over the caramelized onions, close the sandwich, and slice in half.
